<Project>

  <!--
    Solution-wide build settings.

    Security pins for transitive packages flagged by NU1903 (high-severity advisories). Both override a
    vulnerable transitive dependency without changing behaviour; each needs a `dotnet restore` to take
    effect and should be removed once the upstream packages reference patched versions themselves.

    1. System.Security.Cryptography.Xml: the net10 stack resolves a 10.0.x build in the vulnerable
       [10.0.0, 10.0.9] range (CVE-2026-50525 / -50527 / -47304, and the earlier CVE-2026-33116).
       Patched in 10.0.10. (Previous pin was 9.0.15, on the older 9.x line.)

    2. SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3: EF Core SQLite (through 10.0.9) transitively ships 2.1.11, whose
       bundled SQLite is < 3.50.2 (CVE-2025-6965). The upstream fix is slated for EF Core 11; until then
       the accepted workaround is to pin only the native-library package to 3.50.3 — the managed
       SQLitePCLRaw.core/provider stay at 2.1.11, and only the native SQLite binary (stable C ABI) is
       swapped. Remove once Microsoft.Data.Sqlite/EF Core ship a bundle with SQLite >= 3.50.2.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="10.0.10" />
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3" Version="3.50.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
